A **destructor**, written `~Logger()`, runs when an object is destroyed. This `Logger` prints when it is made and when it is destroyed.

```cpp
struct Logger {
    std::string name;
    Logger(std::string n) : name(n) {
        std::cout << "open " << name << '\n';
    }
    ~Logger() { std::cout << "close " << name << '\n'; }
};
```

