Five **special members** decide how an object is copied, moved and destroyed. You choose between two patterns:

```cpp
// rule of zero: members manage themselves
class Buffer {
    std::vector<double> data_;   // write none of the five
};

// rule of five: you own a raw resource
class Handle {
public:
    ~Handle();
    Handle(const Handle&);              // or = delete
    Handle& operator=(const Handle&);   // or = delete
    Handle(Handle&&) noexcept;
    Handle& operator=(Handle&&) noexcept;
};
```

